# P-Ork Gateway — Improvement Backlog

> Context dump from a codebase review (2026-06-08). If you're a future Claude session,
> read this file plus the files it references to get up to speed before implementing any of these.

## What this project is (and what's genuinely good)

P-Ork Gateway is a clean ~2,200-line FastAPI WebSocket gateway that runs the full agentic
loop (LLM ↔ MCP tools) on behalf of P-Ork pipelines. Architecture highlights:

- **Provider abstraction** (`BaseProvider.complete`) normalizes 5 providers (Anthropic native
  + 4 OpenAI/Ollama-compat) onto one `ProviderResponse` shape — `gateway/llm/providers/`.
- **MCP supervision is the standout** — `_monitor` auto-restarts crashed servers and re-caches
  their tools (`gateway/mcp/manager.py:194`), with namespaced tool names (`server__tool`) to
  avoid collisions.
- **Trace streaming** — the runner emits `llm_call`/`thinking`/`tool_call`/`tool_result` events
  live over the same WS frame id (`gateway/runner/agent_runner.py:79`); this powers the live tail.

It works end-to-end and the provider quirk-handling (Ollama putting output in `reasoning`,
native Ollama omitting tool-call IDs) shows real battle-testing.

